            {
                "entry_id": "762274a0-d622-315a-891e-9a47935fb51a",
                "word": "disparate",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "143522b4-0268-47f9-9910-d5615b4cf67c",
                        "entry_id": "762274a0-d622-315a-891e-9a47935fb51a",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "disparates"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5c8da278-a66e-3983-860d-38898b1a8d62",
                        "entry_id": "762274a0-d622-315a-891e-9a47935fb51a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui présente un défaut de conformité d’un effet désagréable."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4458fedc-f508-4818-b3c6-c7e0e5fa0aa5",
                                "sense_id": "5c8da278-a66e-3983-860d-38898b1a8d62",
                                "text": "Encore les taxes qui les frappaient étaient-elles disparates, inégales."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a22a3c0f-48f2-4b42-a33f-161a0bf75920",
                                "sense_id": "5c8da278-a66e-3983-860d-38898b1a8d62",
                                "text": "En arrivant sur la place, avec la ville dans le dos, il y a une dernière rangée de constructions, un peu disparates, des kiosques, des parkings, des manèges, des échoppes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7ca88773-7061-41ee-9832-270d578c3e99",
                                "sense_id": "5c8da278-a66e-3983-860d-38898b1a8d62",
                                "text": "Les militants disparates qui ont saccagé le Capitole ne représentent que les éléments avancés de l’extrême droite armée pro-Trump qui se prépare activement à une deuxième frappe contre les institutions politiques américaines."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8aa8f2e4-f862-3fed-8e45-e03e25f2d766",
                        "entry_id": "762274a0-d622-315a-891e-9a47935fb51a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui n'est pas en accord ou en harmonie avec ce qui l'entoure ; dont la diversité est choquante."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "especially"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a4755e4-ab59-487a-972e-e91c93f58f6a",
                                "sense_id": "8aa8f2e4-f862-3fed-8e45-e03e25f2d766",
                                "text": "Le talent du constructeur s'y révèlera, dès lors, par l'application du principe de la « sincérité dans l'art » : la construction ne sera pas cachée sous des dehors faux ou des ornements disparates et sans but ; […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7849a812-539c-4bf5-8a27-c899cc1e6504",
                                "sense_id": "8aa8f2e4-f862-3fed-8e45-e03e25f2d766",
                                "text": "Je tirai la sonnette ; il se retourna pour me regarder ; son regard fut lent à se détacher de moi. Peut-être trouvait-il qu’avec ma corbeille de primeurs et ma jeunesse relative, je faisais disparate dans le tableau ?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8c6154cb-53aa-4c0d-8a2c-7578e1c7957d",
                        "source_entry_id": "762274a0-d622-315a-891e-9a47935fb51a",
                        "target_lang_word": "disparate",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "disparate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a0493c6f-9291-35b7-92f7-1880333e0b0f",
                                        "entry_id": "fb392ad1-88b4-358c-909d-eb49e32d4570",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Composed of inherently different or distinct elements; incongruous."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b060add-6486-4d49-8cb6-0ba383d4d8ee",
                                                "sense_id": "a0493c6f-9291-35b7-92f7-1880333e0b0f",
                                                "text": "The board of the company was decidedly disparate, with no two members from the same social or economic background."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27fae748-3902-4ab6-aa2d-8190110db7cf",
                                                "sense_id": "a0493c6f-9291-35b7-92f7-1880333e0b0f",
                                                "text": "The London Transport Museum was established, from disparate collections, at Covent Garden in 1980."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1538fb3-b092-4d99-b5dd-54bae86b5554",
                                                "sense_id": "a0493c6f-9291-35b7-92f7-1880333e0b0f",
                                                "text": "Although third-rail operation in the region dates back more than a century, it was in the 1970s that tunnels under Liverpool's city centre opened to bring together previously disparate routes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9c0c5677-0d87-3877-aaf1-ce4d981b6447",
                                        "entry_id": "fb392ad1-88b4-358c-909d-eb49e32d4570",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Essentially different; of different species, unlike but not opposed in pairs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7e5f4a79-107e-326c-9970-215c29845ad0",
                                        "entry_id": "fb392ad1-88b4-358c-909d-eb49e32d4570",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Utterly unlike; incapable of being compared; having no common ground."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8db5861c-e817-41bc-aab1-9b04c3431ea4",
                                                "sense_id": "7e5f4a79-107e-326c-9970-215c29845ad0",
                                                "text": "Then disparate sense impressions come to disparate organs, as light to the eye, taste to the mouth, etc."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28adf696-050c-4ce7-a31b-09df14773f85",
                                                "sense_id": "7e5f4a79-107e-326c-9970-215c29845ad0",
                                                "text": "M. Bergson’s philosophy, unlike most of the systems of the past, is dualistic: the world, for him, is divided into two disparate portions, on the one hand life, on the other matter, or rather that inert something which the intellect views as matter."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "disparate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5c0ba25c-45d9-39be-8518-dd5140951643",
                                        "entry_id": "26d36b49-c492-3dbc-ae43-22371e8ff93b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of a group of unequal or dissimilar things."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "in-plural"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
